<title>USA: Xerox, Ceridian in 5-year deal.</title>
<headline>Xerox, Ceridian in 5-year deal.</headline>
<dateline>EL SEGUNDO, Calif.</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xerox Corp. has a contract worth more than $40 million to supply Ceridian Employer Services with high-speed laser printing systems for producing payroll checks, payroll-related reports and W-2 forms for Ceridian customers, the companies said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The five-year contract includes equipment, service, financing and supplies.</p>
<p>Xerox will be Ceridian's sole print vendor, installing up to 69 Xerox DocuPrint 4635MX laser printing systems in 29 Ceridian district offices.</p>
<p>Xerox's stock rose 75 cents to $54.875 on the New York Stock Exchange in early afternoon trading.</p>
